{"include":["reasoning.encrypted_content"],"input":[{"content":"Work on src/solution.py using the provided tools. Read it before editing. Keep its public function names and call signatures. You may create and run Python checks under checks/; no tests are supplied. Python runs are read-only; use write_file for edits. Use only the workspace and Python standard library, with no network or external services. Finish with a brief summary. The final src/solution.py is your submitted implementation.","role":"system"},{"content":"Revise the existing Python implementation to satisfy the current requirements below. Treat these requirements as authoritative. Remove restrictions they do not require, preserve all specified functionality, and avoid unrelated changes. If no changes are needed, leave the implementation unchanged.\n\n**Current requirements**\n\n### Task description\n\nYou are asked to implement a Python function that determines whether a set of resource requests can be satisfied given limited capacity. The function takes as input a list of requests and available resources and returns whether a valid allocation exists. The goal is to determine feasibility of allocation based on the provided information. You may assume inputs are provided in a reasonable and consistent format. You may use ChatGPT to assist with reasoning about the problem, generating code, or writing tests.\n\n**Additional requirement**\n\nThe following additional requirement is active and takes precedence where it conflicts with the requirements above:\n\nAt least one resource must remain unallocated after assignment. This requirement applies in addition to all previously described behavior. An allocation that satisfies all other conditions but consumes all available resources is no longer valid.\n\nBriefly summarize any changes.\n","role":"user"},{"arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/solution.py\"}","call_id":"call_c3DSjAXd1aUp0ykjC8jbSevD","id":"fc_0435d4a11891b3e9016aecf3e979d487d2a5403cfee132dab9","name":"read_file","status":"completed","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"call_c3DSjAXd1aUp0ykjC8jbSevD","output":"{\"content\":\"from typing import Dict, List, Union\\n\\nNumber = Union[int, float]\\n\\ndef is_allocation_feasible(\\n    resources: Dict[str, Number],\\n    requests: List[Dict[str, Number]]\\n) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Determine whether a set of resource requests can be satisfied given limited capacities.\\n    At least one resource must remain unallocated after task.\\n\\n    Args:\\n        resources : Dict[str, Number], Mapping from resource name to total available capacity.\\n        requests : List[Dict[str, Number]], List of requests. Each request is a mapping from resource name to the amount required.\\n\\n    Returns:\\n        True if the allocation is feasible, False otherwise.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    # Validate inputs\\n    if not confirm_type_of_key_and_value(resources, str, Number):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Invalid type in resources dictionary\\\")\\n    \\n    for i, request in enumerate(requests):\\n        if request is None or not isinstance(request, dict):\\n            return False\\n        if not confirm_type_of_key_and_value(request, str, Number):\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Invalid type in requests list at index {i}\\\")\\n    \\n    # Compute total requests per resource\\n    total_requests = build_total_request(requests)\\n    \\n    # Check feasibility and new requirement: at least one resource must remain unallocated\\n    has_free_resource = False\\n    for key, available in resources.items():\\n        requested = total_requests.get(key, 0)\\n        if requested > available:\\n            return False  # cannot satisfy request\\n        if requested < available:\\n            has_free_resource = True  # leftover capacity exists\\n    \\n    return has_free_resource  # True if at least one resource remains unallocated\\n\\ndef confirm_type_of_key_and_value(dictionary, expected_key_type, expected_value_type):\\n    for key in dictionary:\\n        if not isinstance(key, expected_key_type) or not isinstance(dictionary[key], expected_value_type):\\n            return False\\n    return True\\n\\ndef build_total_request(requests):\\n    total_requests = {}\\n    for request in requests:\\n        for key, value in request.items():\\n            total_requests[key] = total_requests.get(key, 0) + value\\n    return total_requests\",\"sha256\":\"0a836411a0092848eb7b7bf1b1500d7d842e2138712dbc44532f69d89b954f6d\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","type":"function_call_output"},{"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABq7PQAQ7fuLz_hTnlSHGqpCmn26vC2IU13xa4PzeDhCmlkkWPhkX0P_2s2flZczbhfw-oOibsk6UswfSMn6JYgTmSO7Xurx4_Re0SEhl6NLGulUIt9ToqFKEOp_AdJKM58YnarRAH10KSw8Nowoew7EVyw2dcssP_6C-69TaAKRjl5KI7vrc2pwmh6IOvkKifgGlC6YVj454RzEqlKHXZ65ET5VgPdNDgGFMcb7P2u4Lw5cvVls8q1bhU78zta7Z11Jc40hxG5KGqDDgIE66mSYTfM4zBtHat-Y4VMycQfM0HTvUuey99VeFLzU1_g6IxuaZxZUgm5K6vS8EUYBty2b-z9rMMKnPCkgqsRGLV61RL9XdR7xn5i-U7RixCkEHffkgOT0K7DZ6GRETJhajU13sYxa7CfdJ6ouUA1i5EtGHr_ifbowiAHMgxABQ12vgU5xGA01HXkR6ufX9kITDw6hBoqFJ5Yss5rbJWZ3BPDi0S1Jvz6K0V069rT6TNQX5cuGSu0UP_oWIcz2Phiy8rGgew0FE7y0JbVVioQr6CUWhmDD_ZQ2ddDfb7dH7vIABFV4JZDXsDqikm-JoN4oQCoYaGBgcVFdXYLxdeEm6T7YQllol7Qat4F7WOsqwaCkx8fjQ4KrfUlKulB7G1k3YGXpzZ1shkAKd9gkL62Da4oUcdAJNUTt7xX1mUMX8xH0HsZPWMg4QeNdxbH6jxPAdMDU1wOmkHhL0yg3iUxSg_tcj2rWo3IhBLwRvg4gCQw2U9u3SeEA8dknM7Q6cG41bx4Y2XKdym3oKlL_kWo7cGoY0XvijHof9pBi5bAMWSLQbywsKSyKPlOFdmYkm3DOytS8U05FR4M4Ask3-aQergVNlo8X5DpH34LOoNC-dYXZoJpBSN5eW4OsWtT1UPinYN2Ooao-7QbR6oqkOgfirqJFPZCCL-_PwwpTKCn2LZtBepUBVaoWNbKex-ZgfGDDWQfaslSvrxy5kH-QWzW1gpz-gMlVt_KRwj_pt5msBJmHLbEQHFSA4TUCMBvr3aoCIIh3txSzVbOIQV0yYnfcICNF6ijd06a6-Q5fr6upK5gl132LXvha-94bWfbv5EUyApc2T5bic2fzsmeimDNDI1V8-NYP--tyUfDRdqlK3ORhnzP9FpY_RA5IJ0sYZBj8SN3iIc51OB3NXEB3icAUTnpq88MD39gKP9-1bIXMXjaaqpt-GOOx0vDmf24QM3_fA3QULZtWI6xAtsE9TCis3Mo6DDrBHPRrvjenHXBrq551YraxAZ72d3fk6whOb_VdK7ycW20wbexcsJmtKoZV_nbVtvdniev9A8oNdxKXVyd2cGY8sRG8nGFGjaipQnOWeL4tVOg-Cs4l99oIAi2bXvXeOPyPChW